  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f: X \\rightarrow Y$ and $A, B$ are non-void subsets of $Y$, then (where the symbols have their usual interpretation)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9JS6d",
      "text": "$f^{-1}(A)-f^{-1}(B) \\supset f^{-1}(A-B)$ but the opposite does not hold.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "defbX",
      "text": "$f^{-1}(A)-f^{-1}(B) \\subset f^{-1}(A-B)$ but the opposite does not hold.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "xay2l",
      "text": "$f^{-1}(A-B)=f^{-1}(A)-f^{-1}(B)$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "HxAL4",
      "text": "$f^{-1}(A-B)=f^{-1}(A) \\cup f^{-1}(B)$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let A={1,2,3}\r\nand  B={2,3,4}\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2019_mat_a58.png\">\r\nhere, $f^{-1}(3)=1$\r\n$f^{-1}(4)=2$ and $f^{-1}(2)=3$\r\nIt is clear that option (C) $f^{-1}(A-B)=f^{-1}(A)$\r\n$-f^{-1}(B)$ is correct.",
